      "note": "Reviewed the selected transaction receipt and call trace, EFLeverVault and linked-library creation receipts, bytecode at deployment and immediately before the incident, verified source, and commit-pinned reproduction. EFLeverVault 0xe39fd820b58f83205db1d9225f28105971c3d309 is a direct contract with byte-identical runtime at both anchors. Its exploit trace delegates only arithmetic calls to link-time SafeMath 0x071108ad85d7a766b41e0f5e5195537a8fc8e74d, which was deployed earlier and is itself byte-identical across the measurement interval. An external Balancer flash loan invokes receiveFlashLoan(userData=0x2), releasing collateral as ETH because the callback validates Balancer but not who initiated the loan. A subsequent withdraw sends address(this).balance to the helper. The selected transaction withdraws 480.108083265872754211 ETH after a 0.1 ETH seed, establishing a 480.008083265872754211 ETH net loss; the historical 750 ETH figure combines more than this selected transaction."
